<!--
  ============================================================================
  GalacticEmpire.xml                     Jawa_Patches · re-pointed 2026-08-14
                                         renamed 2026-08-20
  ============================================================================

  Builds FACTION_SPEC.md section 1, "Galactic Empire - PATCH vanilla `Empire`",
  under V1_CHAIN R15 and R11.

  🔴 THE VESSEL CHANGED, AND SO DID THE NAME. This file used to reskin
  `OuterRim_GalacticEmpire` into a differently-named sector occupier. ⛔ THAT
  FACTION IS STRUCK FROM THE RECORDS — owner, 2026-08-20: "Doesn't exist
  anymore." Its name is deliberately not repeated here or anywhere else; the
  file was renamed to match on the same day. The Empire is the Galactic Empire
  and has no other name.

  It now patches VANILLA `Empire` (Royalty), and the faction is the Galactic
  Empire. R15's reason is `settlementGenerationWeight`: vanilla `Empire` sits at
  1 against the Outer Rim def's 0.3, which is why the old faction held one
  settlement while the Fallen Dominion held four. The occupier has to outweigh
  the locals to read as one.

  ⚠️ It still references `OuterRim_Imp*` PAWN KINDS under MayRequire, so the
  Neronix17.OuterRim.GalacticEmpire dependency stays. The Outer Rim FACTION def
  is no longer touched.

  READ FROM THE SHIPPED DEF, game up, 2026-08-14 — not inferred:
  C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\RimWorld\Data\Royalty\Defs\
    FactionDefs\Faction_Empire.xml

      ParentName                  FactionBase
      label                       shattered empire
      pawnSingular / pawnsPlural  imperial / imperials
      leaderTitle                 high stellarch
      factionNameMaker            NamerFactionEmpire
      settlementGenerationWeight  1
      techLevel                   Ultra
      fixedName                   ABSENT      -> Add, not Replace
      permanentEnemy              ABSENT      -> Add, not Replace
      fixedLeaderKinds            WRITTEN (line 90) -> Replace, not Add
      pawnGroupMakers             [1] Trader · [2] Combat commonality 100 ·
                                  [3] Combat commonality 10 · [4] Settlement

  ⚠️ `fixedName` IS AN ADD. Vanilla `Empire` has no `fixedName` node at all;
  it names itself through `NamerFactionEmpire`, which generates a random name.
  A `Replace` here would match nothing and log a red error. The spec REQUIRES
  the world to say "Galactic Empire", so the node has to be created.

  ⚠️ Do NOT patch `factionNameMaker` away. `fixedName` overrides it for the
  faction itself, and the namer is still what names the faction's SETTLEMENTS.

  ⚠️ techLevel is left alone. The spec's "Spacer (vessel default)" mis-reads the
  vessel — it actually ships `Ultra` — but the instruction is "no change", so
  no change is what this file makes.

  🔑 THE COMBAT GROUPS ARE NAMED BY THEIR COMMONALITY, NOT BY POSITION. A positional
  predicate would be correct today and wrong the moment any mod inserts a group ahead
  of ours; `[commonality="100"]` cannot drift. It is also the form both engines agree
  on — ElementTree's `[N]` counts siblings by tag while XPath 1.0's counts the nodes
  the previous predicate kept, so `li[kindDef="Combat"][1]` reads as DEAD under a
  findall()-based checker while RimWorld's System.Xml resolves it correctly.

  ⛔ COMBAT GROUPS ONLY. `pawnGroupMakers/li[kindDef="Combat"]` is TWO nodes on
  this def, so each op carries a positional predicate on the filtered set. The
  Trader and Settlement groups are untouched by design: they carry the
  Royalty trade and settlement pawns, which are not part of R15.

  🔑 THE RAID IS OURS NOW — IMPERIAL_RAID_ROSTER_1, 2026-08-21. Both combat
  groups were built out of Outer Rim's `OuterRim_ImpStorm*` line troops, and the
  four Imperial kinds this mod authors in
  `Defs/PawnKindDefs/JawaFactionRoster.xml` had NO SPAWN ROUTE AT ALL:
  `defaultFactionDef` names the faction a kind belongs to, it does not put the
  kind in a raid. Only a `pawnGroupMaker` does. So the three fighting kinds now
  carry both groups:

      Jawa_Empire_Grunt        5      stormtrooper,     combatPower  87
      Jawa_Empire_Heavy        2      heavy trooper,    combatPower 129
      Jawa_Empire_Specialist   1.5    Imperial officer, combatPower 119

  and the fourth, `Jawa_Empire_Leader` (Emperor Palpatine, combatPower 211), is
  wired in through `fixedLeaderKinds` above rather than through a group, because
  a leader is generated once for the faction and not rolled into raids.

  The three Outer Rim SPECIALISTS stay in the RARE group only
  (`OuterRim_ImpRangeTrooper`, `_ImpDeathTrooper`, `_ImpISBAgent`, all
  combatPower 200), mirroring vanilla's own split where the commonality-10 group
  carries the heavier option list. They are kept because they are flavour the
  authored four do not carry. None of them holds the 99999 exclude-from-raid
  sentinel; checked, all three are 200.

  ⚠️ Our three kinds stay INSIDE the Outer Rim `PatchOperationFindMod` even
  though they are ours, and that is deliberate: `Jawa_Empire_Grunt` declares
  `apparelRequired` on `OuterRim_StormtrooperCuirass` and
  `OuterRim_StormtrooperHelmet`, so without that mod the whole group is wrong
  anyway.

  ⛔ Do NOT touch the Trader or Settlement groups. They keep Royalty's villagers,
  janissaries and cataphracts by design === FACTION_SPEC.md:130, EMPIRE_GAP_AUDIT.md
  section 3.

  SAFETY
  ======
  Everything is inside a conditional on the Empire def existing, so the file is
  a silent no-op without Royalty rather than a wall of red. The group-maker ops
  additionally sit inside a `PatchOperationFindMod` for Outer Rim - Galactic
  Empire, and every Imperial defName also carries `MayRequire`, because an
  unwrapped defName from a disabled mod is a silent no-op that reads as success.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Empire"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <!-- "shattered empire" -> the occupier's own name. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Empire"]/label</xpath>
          <value><label>The Galactic Empire</label></value>
        </li>

        <!-- REQUIRED. Absent on the vessel; NamerFactionEmpire would otherwise
             generate a random name and the world must say Galactic Empire. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Empire"]</xpath>
          <value><fixedName>Galactic Empire</fixedName></value>
        </li>

        <!-- high stellarch -> Emperor (R11). -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Empire"]/leaderTitle</xpath>
          <value><leaderTitle>Emperor</leaderTitle></value>
        </li>

        <!--
          The leader the world actually names. WRITTEN on the vessel
          (Data/Royalty/Defs/FactionDefs/Faction_Empire.xml:90, one li holding
          Empire_Royal_Stellarch), so this is a REPLACE. An Add here would
          append a second li and the Stellarch would keep rolling half the time.

          OUTSIDE the Outer Rim FindMod on purpose: Jawa_Empire_Leader is ours,
          shipped in this same mod, and needs no third-party gate.
        -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Empire"]/fixedLeaderKinds</xpath>
          <value>
            <fixedLeaderKinds>
              <li>Jawa_Empire_Leader</li>
            </fixedLeaderKinds>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!--
          ================================================================
          THE IMPERIAL WORD FOR IT === IMPERIAL_VOCABULARY_KEYED_1
          ================================================================
          `royalFavorLabel` on the vessel is literally `honor`, and it is the
          string the engine splices into every reward line, every quest
          description and the Factions tab toggle. WRITTEN on the vessel
          (Faction_Empire.xml:16 and :17), so BOTH of these are Replaces.

          🔑 `Empire` is the ONLY def in the whole 578-mod load set that carries
          `royalFavorLabel` or `royalTitleTags` === checked against the def dump,
          not assumed. So the Keyed overrides that ship beside this file cannot
          mistranslate somebody else's faction; there is nobody else.

          "Imperial favor", not "favour": RimWorld's own UI is US English and the
          label renders inline with shipped strings. The design prose
          (faction_world_spec.md:334, tidally_locked_world.md:274) writes
          "imperial favour" and this is that phrase, spelled to match its
          neighbours.

          ⚠️ The ICON is half the fix and it is easy to skip. Left alone it keeps
          pointing at `UI/Icons/RoyalFavor`, Royalty's crown, next to the new
          word. It is re-pointed at the faction badge this mod already ships and
          already uses for `factionIconPath` ===
          `Textures/World/JawaFactions/GalacticEmpire.png`, 128x128 RGBA, on disk.
          No new art, and the badge and the currency read as one faction.

          ⚠️ NOT a rename of what the currency DOES. The player cannot earn it:
          the Empire is a permanent enemy, so titles, permits and the bestowing
          quests are dark by design (EMPIRE_GAP_AUDIT.md section 3). This item is
          about the strings that still render anyway.
        -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Empire"]/royalFavorLabel</xpath>
          <value><royalFavorLabel>Imperial favor</royalFavorLabel></value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Empire"]/royalFavorIconPath</xpath>
          <value><royalFavorIconPath>World/JawaFactions/GalacticEmpire</royalFavorIconPath></value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Empire"]/pawnSingular</xpath>
          <value><pawnSingular>stormtrooper</pawnSingular></value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Empire"]/pawnsPlural</xpath>
          <value><pawnsPlural>stormtroopers</pawnsPlural></value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Empire"]/description</xpath>
          <value>
            <description>The occupier, and the only permanent enemy. Not hateful — procedural. Standardised infantry moved by drop-pod, security droids that were requisitioned rather than chosen, the rare Sith attached to nothing anyone can name, and a reach that is mostly orbital.\n\nIt does not want this world. It wants what leaves this world on schedule.</description>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!--
          Pillar 5: the Galactic Empire alone is the permanent enemy - but it is
          permanently hostile to a NAMED SET, not to the whole planet.
          Owner's ruling 2026-08-20, "Option (b) please";
          design/Jawa/worldbuilding/EMPIRE_GAP_AUDIT.md section 2 carries the
          reasoning for every entry.

          permanentEnemy is set FALSE rather than removed, and that is not a
          style choice. FactionDef.PermanentlyHostileTo tests it FIRST:

              if (permanentEnemy) return true;
              if (permanentEnemyToEveryoneExcept != null
                  && !permanentEnemyToEveryoneExcept.Contains(otherFactionDef))
                  return true;

          so leaving it true returns before the list is ever read and makes the
          whole whitelist dead code. ABSENT on the vessel, so this is an Add.
        -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Empire"]</xpath>
          <value><permanentEnemy>false</permanentEnemy></value>
        </li>

        <!--
          THE WHITELIST, and read the direction before editing it: this lists who
          is NOT a permanent enemy. Anything absent from it IS one.

          PRESENT on the vessel (Faction_Empire.xml line 57), so this is a
          Replace, not an Add.

          The shipped list carries PlayerTribe and PlayerColony. Both are
          DELIBERATELY DROPPED here, and that single omission is what keeps the
          Empire permanently hostile to the player - the owner's 2026-08-14
          ruling. Also dropped, also deliberately: Jawa_FreeDroidEnclaves,
          Jawa_GeonosianFoundryHive, Jawa_WildsteamClan and Jawa_AscendantHelix.
          Do not "helpfully" restore any of the six.
        -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Empire"]/permanentEnemyToEveryoneExcept</xpath>
          <value>
            <permanentEnemyToEveryoneExcept>
              <li>Jawa_HuttCartel</li>
              <li>Jawa_DeepwaterCompact</li>
              <li>Jawa_IndigenousTribes</li>
              <li>Jawa_Junkers</li>
              <li>OutlanderCivil</li>
              <li>TribeCivil</li>
              <li>Pirate</li>
              <li>Ancients</li>
              <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">Beggars</li>
              <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Anomaly">ResearchExpedition</li>
              <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">GravshipCrew</li>
              <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">TradersGuild</li>
            </permanentEnemyToEveryoneExcept>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!-- 1 -> 0.45. Three surface settlements by design; the other seven or
             eight are orbital fiction the map never has to draw. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Empire"]/settlementGenerationWeight</xpath>
          <value><settlementGenerationWeight>0.45</settlementGenerationWeight></value>
        </li>

        <!--
          ================================================================
          THE RISING ORDER — faction_religions_spec.md entry 1 (B54)
          ================================================================
          Authored, not constrained. Vanilla `Empire` ships `requiredMemes` +
          `structureMemeWeights`, which STEER a generated religion; both are
          removed here because `fixedIdeo` means "do not generate", which makes
          them dead weight that only invites a later contradiction.

          `ideoName` and `ideoDescription` are copied VERBATIM from the spec —
          they are the only strings the engine renders, and the Empire's
          contempt for the player's faith now lives in that description and
          nowhere else, because every precept that could have carried it
          measured unreachable.

          ⛔ `hiddenIdeo` MUST STAY UNSET. Setting it suppresses the description
          entirely, which is the whole deliverable.

          `Structure_TheistEmbodied` has deityCount 2-4, so `deityPresets` is
          mandatory and two are given. Four normal memes is exactly the
          `MemeCountRangeAbsolute` ceiling — the ceiling is a COUNT, never an
          impact budget. Structure meme goes FIRST in `forcedMemes`.
        -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationRemove">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Empire"]/requiredMemes</xpath>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationRemove">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Empire"]/structureMemeWeights</xpath>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Empire"]</xpath>
          <value>
            <fixedIdeo>true</fixedIdeo>
            <requiredPreceptsOnly>true</requiredPreceptsOnly>
            <ideoName>The Rising Order</ideoName>
            <ideoDescription>We have never seen him. We will never see him. He is rising, and we are the ground he rises from. Take the helmet: it is the last thing you will ever choose. There is no doubt among us — only disorder, and disorder is corrected. Say the name once when you are given the armour, and once when you are taken out of it. Between those two words, stand in line.</ideoDescription>
            <forcedMemes>
              <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">Structure_TheistEmbodied</li>
              <li MayRequire="vanillaexpanded.vmemese">VME_GodEmperor</li>
              <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">Proselytizer</li>
              <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">Supremacist</li>
              <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">HumanPrimacy</li>
            </forcedMemes>
            <styles>
              <li MayRequire="vanillaexpanded.vmemese">VME_Authoritarian</li>
              <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">Techist</li>
            </styles>
            <deityPresets>
              <li>
                <nameType><name>Palpatine</name><type>He Who Is Rising</type></nameType>
                <gender>Male</gender>
                <iconPath>UI/Deities/DeityGeneric</iconPath>
              </li>
              <li>
                <nameType><name>the Line</name><type>That Which Has No Face</type></nameType>
                <gender>None</gender>
                <iconPath>UI/Deities/DeityGeneric</iconPath>
              </li>
            </deityPresets>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!-- R15: stormtroopers, not cataphracts. Combat groups only. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
          <mods>
            <li>Outer Rim - Galactic Empire</li>
          </mods>
          <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
            <operations>

              <!-- The common raid (vanilla commonality 100). Line troops only. -->
              <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
                <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Empire"]/pawnGroupMakers/li[kindDef="Combat"][commonality="100"]/options</xpath>
                <value>
                  <options>
                    <Jawa_Empire_Grunt>5</Jawa_Empire_Grunt>
                    <Jawa_Empire_Heavy>2</Jawa_Empire_Heavy>
                    <Jawa_Empire_Specialist>1.5</Jawa_Empire_Specialist>
                  </options>
                </value>
              </li>

              <!-- The rare raid (vanilla commonality 10). Line troops plus the
                   three 200-power specialists. -->
              <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
                <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Empire"]/pawnGroupMakers/li[kindDef="Combat"][commonality="10"]/options</xpath>
                <value>
                  <options>
                    <Jawa_Empire_Grunt>5</Jawa_Empire_Grunt>
                    <Jawa_Empire_Heavy>2</Jawa_Empire_Heavy>
                    <Jawa_Empire_Specialist>1.5</Jawa_Empire_Specialist>
                    <OuterRim_ImpRangeTrooper MayRequire="Neronix17.OuterRim.GalacticEmpire">2</OuterRim_ImpRangeTrooper>
                    <OuterRim_ImpDeathTrooper MayRequire="Neronix17.OuterRim.GalacticEmpire">1.5</OuterRim_ImpDeathTrooper>
                    <OuterRim_ImpISBAgent MayRequire="Neronix17.OuterRim.GalacticEmpire">1</OuterRim_ImpISBAgent>
                  </options>
                </value>
              </li>

        <!-- Bespoke world-map icon. the def writes it - Data/Royalty/Defs/FactionDefs/Faction_Empire.xml:19, so REPLACE. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Empire"]/factionIconPath</xpath>
          <value><factionIconPath>World/JawaFactions/GalacticEmpire</factionIconPath></value>
        </li>

            </operations>
          </match>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
